  "7#_": "(Taz s.k. 3) This is not called two flaws. Here according to Rashi's view that there is no adhesion without puncture — except that the ona's lining helps — we say well that even though emerging from bubble which is two flaws and indicates puncture — in any case we know there is puncture; except the ona seals (except according to Maharshal brought in Shach s.k. 2 that on account of protruding bubble it does not adhere well). But according to Tosafot's view the ona does not seal, rather the adhesion did not come from puncture — if so one may say emerging from within the bubble which is two flaws — we judge for puncture and it is forbidden; except one may say it is not certainly two flaws, for perhaps the adhesion emerges from another ona; if so if there are two bubbles opposite one another and adhesion emerges from both bubbles — treifah according to Tosafot; and likewise with two bubbles and adjacent and adhesion emerging from them in order — treifah.",
