export const sifteiKohen = {
  "1#_": "And many permit even murky, etc. Meaning even in bubbles of mugla that are murky and putrid — likewise; and so is implied from poskim and acharonim and is simple; and even though above siman 36 seif 7 regarding lung poured out the Rav ruled in the hagahah that only in great loss one may permit murky and putrid — one may say that there too there is also concern for bronchi requiring examination whether they melted; and see s.k. 26 and s.k. 30.",
  "2#א": "If an adhesion hangs out, etc. As Beit Yosef wrote in the name of Raavad that if an adhesion hangs emerging from the bubble — forbidden, and even in an ona we do not say the lining protects it, etc.; as Beit Yosef wrote, and I do not know the reason for the matter, for behold we say lung punctured and lining seals it — kosher; and Rokeach wrote similarly that if there is adhesion of a thread in a bubble — declare treifah; and it is possible he speaks not in a place of protrusion — end; however below siman 39 he brought Raavad's words at length and it is explained there his reason: we say in the Gemara specifically when it is matted in the flesh it is kosher when the lining seals; but here it is not matted and did not adhere, etc. — see there; and so Bach and Lev Chaim daf 155a explained; and Beit Yosef himself retracted in his Beit Yosef book and Bach and Lev Chaim did not see his words in Beit Yosef — see there; and accordingly all the more for us who hold the lining never protects, as written in hagahah siman 39 seif 18 treifah; and so the Gaon z\"l wrote in responsum and expanded in clear great proofs greater than this from Maharshal Perek Aleph Tav siman 44 who wrote even nowadays kosher as matted; and ruled in siman 28 like Raavad because we do not say lining protects — and this is their protrusion; except regarding division of lung which then adheres well — unlike protruding bubble.",
  "2#ב": "Emerging from the bubble. From \"and sealed\" it implies even a bubble of clear water; and so from Maharshal Perek Aleph Tav siman 28; however one may say they follow their reason who declare treifah adjacent in clear water; and so the R\"tz wrote in the name of the Azrieli that clear water is not considered a flaw neither for adjacency nor for hanging adhesion emerging from it and not adhered elsewhere; and such is custom — end; and so Bach wrote that for one who permits adjacent in clear water, all the more he permits hanging adhesion from bubble in clear water; and Maharam in his Beit Yosef book challenged the Azrieli and R\"tz on this and his view is to declare treifah in adhesion emerging from bubble of clear water even for one who permits adjacent in clear water; and all his words are not compelling at all — see there; also what he wrote in the name of Mahariv and Maharam to forbid — no proof, for it is clear in their words they forbade in adjacency; and see responsum Ben Lev part 3 siman 100.",
  "2#ג": "And the same applies to bubble, etc. Meaning as adhesion emerging from bubble is treifah because it is two flaws — if so the same on protrusion and the like; and what is protrusion was explained siman 35 seif 5 in the hagahah.",
  "2#ד": "On protrusion. But if it changes to lung appearance — kosher — end; Machatzit HaShekel wrote in several places; and it appears he means if the skin of the bubble changes to lung appearance even though it stands on protrusion or other flaw — kosher, for since it has lung appearance it is only internal deficiency.",
  "3#א": "Adjacent, etc. forbidden. Rashi explained the reason: we hold they are adjacent only on account of puncture in the lung that raised the blisters; and Raah agreed in Beit Yosef daf 34; and Rambam ch. 7 explained because the matter is close that there are punctures between them and they have no way of examination; and Rashba and Ran and Rabbeinu Yerucham explained since they are adjacent to one another, because each presses its fellow, eventually the skin will puncture and it is as if punctured now; and in those types that are kosher — two adjacent bubbles — these reasons do not apply.",
  "3#ב": "If they pour. Maharshal wrote Perek Aleph Tav siman 27 in the name of Maharil that even when pouring examination is required to see if each has a pouch by itself; if in two pouches with a break between — treifah, for since there is puncture between them that pour to one another — we fear puncture of lung, for from place of lung the blister arose, only afterward they drew near — and it is like membrane that arose from blow on lung and is not membrane — end; and so in Hagahot Mordechai — two adjacent bubbles have no examination even when pouring; and so implied in examinations of R\"tz regarding what Machatzit HaShekel wrote: every bubble has a pouch and lies in it; and two bubbles appearing as one — puncture one and they pour to one another — certainly lung punctured between the two bubbles and treifah, etc. — see there (except he did not mention examination is required l'chatchila); and so appears the Rav's view and as written s.k. 33 and in Machberet HaChayim he wrote from Tosafot that from break of two hairs it is not considered adjacent — implies if no proper gap and they pour — kosher; his words are astonishing, for on the contrary from their writing \"not considered adjacent\" implies when no two hairs between — considered adjacent; and regarding adjacent it is certain even pouring — treifah, for otherwise Rava and poskim need not say one appearing as two; and so necessarily as we said.",
  "3#ג": "Tzemachim, etc. They are called in Shas and poskim tinnir; and in responsum of the Rav simanim 5, 6, 7 a dispute was found with Maharshal — Maharshal's view: tinnir means hard with a little moisture, for if no moisture at all it is sealed as explained above siman 37 seif 9; and the Rav's view: even if no moisture at all, only completely hard like stone — nevertheless since its appearance resembles mugla appearance it is tinnir, as written in hagahah siman 36; and see there in responsum where he explained his reason; and so in examinations of acharonim.",
  "3#ד": "Hard. Bach wrote: it appears the same when full of air — kosher in adjacent — end; and it appears proof, for poskim who declare treifah in clear water in adjacent only forbid from the reason the language of bubble applies — \"water requested,\" as in Rosh; if so when full of air one cannot say thus.",
  "3#ה": "And the same applies to morsa, etc. In all books this hagahah is written after \"and these are when there is mugla or water in them\"; therefore Lev Chaim daf 157a wrote in the name of Mahariu: morsa on lung — meaning lung membrane covers it and it is not higher than lung flesh — its law is like bubble with mugla that is treifah — end; and I did not stand on the end of his view, for the matter is simple it is a scribal error and this hagahah belongs after \"but if they are tzemachim,\" etc. (and he answered: thus I hagah'd also in my Shulchan Aruch many years ago — end); and so explicitly in Mahariu and Darkei Moshe and Maharshal there and Bach — it is not a bubble to forbid in adjacency when lung membrane covers it, etc.; and Maharshal agreed there with correct reasons — see there; and so in Taz and Api Ravrevi and other acharonim.",
  "3#ו": "That lung membrane covers, etc. Maharam wrote in Beit Yosef: morsa means what they call in Italian the appearance of moisture inside like precious stone called turquoise; they grow between skin and flesh even though membrane covering them has no lung appearance — only morsa appearance — kosher; but bubbles are normally inside flesh and are rot of flesh — therefore there flesh thread surrounding is required, etc. — see there; and it is not clear — if so if lung membrane does not cover them, are they adjacent and treifah? And so Rashba and R\"tz whom I brought s.k. 28 — bubbles of Gemara are those growing between skin and flesh — \"two adjacent\" treifah; also we find no posek who distinguished — rather truth of the matter used term morsa, for presumably they are not accustomed to be higher than lung flesh; and so Maharshal Perek Aleph Tav siman 27 explained.",
  "3#ז": "And it is not high, etc. And he wrote in Torat HaShelamim there: but if higher than measure of tarfa de-asa and has form of ona — forbids on account of extra — end; his words are astonishing, for what connection to extra of ona; rather simply he means if high — forbids on account of adjacency; therefore even if no tarfa de-asa and no ona form — forbids in adjacency.",
  "3#ח": "Like two hairs. And Maharshal there ruled we require gap width of kesh; we are not expert between one hair and two; and poskim agreed to be lenient.",
  "3#ט": "Lung appearance. Meaning to exclude mugla appearance; for even if among permitted appearances that will be explained siman 38 — since mugla quartered beneath it — it is adjacent.",
  "3#י": "And sweet. To exclude bitter or salty which are like murky — Mahariu there; and found in examinations of acharonim — see there Ram siman \"what is clear water\": whatever has a pouch by itself and peels from lung and no air exits when puncturing the bubble; and bubble skin is white inside — end; and it appears this sign was needed because Mahara\"k root 36 wrote in name of Tosafot Rif that nowadays we are not expert between clear and murky — therefore they gave a sign even for us; and Semachot strained on this.",
  "3#כ": "Custom, etc. Or according to matter of loss. And Maharshal there disagrees with custom and his view appears one may not permit even in great loss; and truly for law the words of forbidders are primary; and also according to primary reason that one presses its fellow — no distinction; and Bach wrote one who is stringent for himself — examine; therefore it appears what the Rav wrote \"or according to loss and time of pressure\" — specifically where both exist; not as Pri Megadim who wrote \"or time of pressure.\"",
  "3#ל": "Their law like adjacent. Meaning where they practice prohibition in clear water in adjacent — the same in slopes; and where they practice permission; but regarding surrounding thread it is not similar, for all agree in slopes one hair suffices as s.k. 22; and see s.k. 28.",
  "3#מ": "Bubble on groove. On upper ona of right in place of groove — so in Machatzit HaShekel there.",
  "3#נ": "For it is like two bubbles, etc. And accordingly in clear water one may be lenient where lenient; and Semachot wrote another reason — concern friction of bubbles on small ribs and gargeret — good to be stringent.",
  "3#ס": "Between two onot — kosher. For there is gap between them; and even for reason one presses its fellow — nevertheless since onot are normally separate in animal's life they do not press one another.",
  "4#א": "In slopes, etc. This law has no root in Gemara — only from BeHag; poskim strained to find reason to settle his words because all his words are received tradition; and primary reason as Sefer HaChinuch and Semag and Hagahot Mordechai and other poskim — because it appears like two adjacent bubbles and concern for marit ayin; therefore they permitted tinnir in slopes.",
  "4#ב": "Any amount. Implies even one hair-thread; and so Maharshal wrote; and so in examinations of acharonim.",
  "4#ג": "And it must be surrounding, etc. And so in examinations of acharonim; and implies to exclude other appearances even permitted appearances below siman 38; unlike R' Tanchum at end of examinations of R\"tz and Maharshal there who wrote in one hagahah that flesh-thread lung appearance is not needed; and he agreed since one hair suffices — if so certainly this has no lung appearance; and further since many geonim permit bubble in slopes — one may be lenient — end.",
  "4#ד": "And if there was no surrounding, etc. Bach answered R' Yosef son of Rosh on an incident: two examined lung and saw bubble in slopes and agreed no flesh surrounded after inflation; afterward examiners came, inflated, permitted, tore bubble and said those who inflated before had better strength than first — therefore flesh surrounded; establish two against two; animal slaughtered in presumption of permission stands; rely on them that flesh surrounded and permitted — so Beit Yosef brought siman 39 and Beit Yosef agreed. However for us who are stringent to declare treifah animal not examined — animal stands in presumption of prohibition and forbidden; and so Maharshal Perek Kama of Chullin siman 21 — end. One may wonder he skipped R' Yosef son of Rosh's words — Beit Yosef brought his language there; also bubble in slopes was not mentioned except from the Gaon, not in Gemara; also \"establish two\" — if so even without reason of establish two — permit from reason that bubble in slopes is only from Gaon; and we do not add on it — specifically where we know certainly no surrounding thread; and further there is no contradiction in witnesses — perhaps last forgot better than first; and Maharshal deals explicitly with contradiction in adhesion, not slopes; also according to what below siman 39 s.k. 42 Maharshal's words do not exist — all the more here permitted, for we hold animal slaughtered in presumption of permission stands; and so Darkei Moshe brought responsum of R' Yosef and Beit Yosef in general.",
  "5#א": "Even though they do not pour, etc. In Hagahot Maimoniyot it is explained it is more reasonable to permit when not pouring — he wrote it appears to permit if not pouring, etc.; and so R' Shmuel HaLevi ruled and saw they do not pour and permitted — end; and Beit Yosef brings it; and the reason is when pouring, since it happened so much it resembles poured like a pitcher and there is concern for bronchi (and so Mahariu, Mahara\"k, and other acharonim); and one must say the Mechaber holds it is more reasonable to declare treifah when not pouring because it appears like two adjacent bubbles; and it appears to him thus from Hagahot Maimoniyot there; and people practiced to permit bubble across whether pouring or not, for it does not appear like two adjacent bubbles pouring to one another — end; it appears the doubt was it appears like two adjacent — and that is specifically when not pouring — requires study.",
  "5#ב": "Kosher, etc. And written in Beit Yosef: however where it stands opposite bronchi it appears we are concerned for Rambam's words and examine the bronchus between them — end; and the Rav implies he declares treifah and examination does not help; and so from other acharonim who closed their words; and so Maharshal Perek Aleph Tav siman 37 — in large bubble (full of mugla or murky water; but clear water Maharshal permits in great loss through examination — see there) in place of bronchi and across — expert examination does not help even in great loss since we are not expert in examination — end; and so from the Rav's words — even in great loss he declares treifah since he did not distinguish; but difficult, for above siman 36 seif 7 regarding lung poured like a pitcher he wrote even murky and putrid kosher through examination in great loss; and one may say the Rav holds here this bronchus examination is pouring into vessel and seeing white threads — if melted; if not, not melted as there — and specifically poured like pitcher without bubble; but here since there is bubble and bubbles raise rot inside, perhaps bronchi melted inside and rotted until appearance of moisture in bubble changed — therefore impossible to see white threads in vessel — therefore treifah in every case; and I proved below s.k. 28 from Hagahot Mordechai and Mahara\"k — see there.",
  "5#ג": "Thin, etc. Meaning in general in animals we say these are their measures; but if we see bronchi outside these measures — treifah — so Semachot; but in Lev Chaim daf 156a it is written it implies we do not care to fear bronchi at edge outside these measures.",
  "5#ד": "And even clear water. And Maharshal there permits clear water in great loss through examination; and wrote his reason: it is reasonable in clear water they did not melt; and further it is extra stringency and most poskim did not mention it; also Rosh and Tur did not mention — end his language; and it appears to me bubble across has place in Gemara and agreed by all poskim — lung poured like a pitcher where bronchi stand; if so all the more bubble across where it stands in place of bronchi; and if so what is lacking because it protrudes — after all there is internal deficiency like poured; and on the contrary bubble is worse than poured, for it protrudes and lung membrane does not cover it (and poured deals even in clear water as all poskim prove — see there); and so Maharam from whom this law's source — he derived this from lung poured like a pitcher as in responsum of Maharam (Prague edition) siman 66 and Mordechai and Teshuvot HaTaz and Mahara\"k root 36 and other acharonim; and so found in hagahot in name of Mahariu in his work to declare treifah bubble across even in clear water; and Maharshal brings it there; and so Agudah; and so proven explicitly from Rashba and Ran whom Beit Yosef brings — they challenged Rambam that every bubble requires examining bronchus beneath it, learned from poured like pitcher — not clear that only for poured because inside flesh melted; but in large bubbles between skin and flesh we do not fear bronchus puncture — end their language implies explicitly in bubbles inside across, not between skin and flesh, we fear bronchi; and what Maharshal wrote most poskim did not mention law of bubble across — it is nothing, for it is included in lung poured like pitcher and is worse; and Beit Yosef ruled thus that across requires examination — as I brought his language at beginning s.k. 26. And truly at first glance I wondered on Hagahot Maimoniyot that custom permits bubble across — behold it is worse than poured and melted lung; and on what Mahara\"k inclined to be lenient in bubble across since Semag, Semak, Rashba, and other poskim did not mention it — behold it is included in poured and melted and is worse; and it appears clear even Hagahot Mordechai and Mahara\"k only say to permit through bronchus examination; and accordingly the Mechaber also wrote in general to permit and necessarily deals through examination as s.k. mentioned; and forbidders in Hagahot Mordechai hold here examination does not help, unlike poured; and so Mahara\"k wanted to forbid even through examination — as written for the Rav's view there.",
  "5#ה": "But not pouring, etc. And the reason: then it is not similar to poured like a pitcher and there is no concern for bronchi.",
  "5#ו": "Even murky, etc. And even though above siman 36 seif 7 hagahah wrote specifically in great loss one may permit murky and putrid — there because poured like pitcher from side to side and from concern for bronchi as s.k. 1; but here since they do not pour to one another — not similar to poured like a pitcher and no concern for bronchi at all.",
  "5#ז": "Bubble under varda, etc. And so Mahariu and examinations of acharonim; and Maharshal Perek Aleph Tav siman 38 brought divided views and decided even in varda one declares treifah only when no flesh thread surrounding.",
  "5#ח": "Tinnir, etc. And Maharshal there siman 37 disagreed because treifah across is extra stringency; and we do not add on it; and nevertheless one may be lenient in tinnir for we find no bronchus concern except in poured; and so examinations of acharonim and Semachot — such is practice.",
  "5#ט": "And see above siman 42. Meaning there seif 5 regarding two marot it is explained: if they punctured and did not pour and afterward inflated this one and its fellow rose in inflation, or they put water in one and thereby its fellow filled — called pouring to one another; and the same here; and it appears the Rav did not write thus above regarding adjacent because he holds as Maharshal and R\"tz s.k. 7 — see there.",
  "6#א": "Where slaughterer's hand did not feel. But where he felt — we rely on him to be lenient.",
  "6#ב": "Treifah. And we do not surround bubbles as we surround lung as above siman 36 seif 5 — bubbles are apt to change.",
};

export const tureiZahav = {
  "1#_": "And many permit. Meaning even in very large bubbles and they were not concerned for bronchus examination; and so Maharshal.",
  "2#א": "If adhesion hangs out, etc. Maharshal explained the reason: since there is no adhesion without puncture in such a case where flaw is before us and adhesion emerges from it — end; and hanging adhesion — see siman 39 seif 8. And it appears all the more if there is complete adhesion — adhered elsewhere and emerging from bubble — treifah; and what they practice to press and feel adhesions does not help here, as siman 39 seif 13 — for hanging adhesion is permitted for all, yet forbidden when emerging from bubble; a fortiori adhered adhesion whom many poskim do not permit with any pressing; it is simple one must declare treifah for all where there is further flaw — emerging from bubble, and even from tinnir — it appears treifah and pressing does not help as siman 39 seif 8.",
  "2#ב": "And the same bubble standing, etc. From this examiners learned to declare treifah wherever there are two flaws; and not similar to hanging adhesion from tinnir which is kosher as siman 39 seif 8 — tinnir has no flaw there at all; and in hagahot of R\"tz on examinations he wrote hanging adhesion from bubble with clear water — kosher, for clear water is not a flaw at all; and it appears to me treifah here, for Tosafot Perek Aleph Tav daf 43 \"he will split\" wrote clear water is a flaw and kosher — found here treifah from force of two flaws; and Moharach z\"l also wrote likewise one who permits two adjacent bubbles in clear water as seif 3 — the same kosher here; and it appears different there, for only one flaw — whatever you say clear water is flaw is kosher, you have no disqualification even from adjacency; unlike here two flaws, each independent — hanging adhesion is flaw by itself and bubble of clear water is flaw by itself — combination declares treifah; and so I saw in Machberet HaChayim on examinations — R\"tz wrote his law in name of Azrieli; this matter is not in Azrieli's book at all, for I searched and it is not there. It appears bubble emerging from adhesion between ona and ona below halfway — this is not called two flaws, for below halfway there is no adhesion on it at all; however if there is window — even though we permit as below siman 39 seif 4 — nevertheless since poskim declare treifah even there in window, and here there is further bubble flaw — at least called two flaws and treifah; and so if bubble emerges from adhesion between ona and ama below halfway even without window — since some poskim hold that adhesion treifah though we do not hold thus — nevertheless here called two flaws — so appears to me. Incident before me: lung adhered to pouch and adhesion full of blood until where adhesion to pouch all around filled with blood appearance — I declared treifah, for here worse than two flaws — pressing and feeling do not help, for I say it is only spreading of this blood's moisture from lung punctured and blood exited from its bronchi — spreading of moisture certainly occurs even if not punctured — unlike this blood; and even though it does not bubble — treifah, for examination does not help to permit where prohibition is doubtful — as siman 39 seif 4.",
  "3#א": "Adjacent to one another. Rashi's reason: we hold they are adjacent only from puncture in lung that raised these blisters; Rashba and Ran — since adjacent they press and eventually puncture — as if punctured now. Except what Rama wrote shortly bubble and tinnir kosher — implies like Rashi's view, not Rashba.",
  "3#ב": "One and kosher. Maharshal wrote in name of Maharil — still requires examination whether each has pouch by itself — treifah.",
  "3#ג": "But if they are tzemachim, etc. Meaning there is no moisture at all — this is called tinnir.",
  "3#ד": "And the same morsa, etc. This hagahah belongs elsewhere even though adjacent kosher; Maharshal gave reason morsa kosher — not called bubble but protruding outward; and implies there is mugla in this morsa — nevertheless does not forbid in adjacency.",
  "3#ה": "And it must be in what separates. Meaning not kosher when there is gap unless lung appearance; but if mugla appearance — like adjacent; Machatzit HaShekel: if upper skin of bubble peeled — lung skin — treifah, for lower skin is bubble skin from blow — even single bubble, even clear water.",
  "3#ו": "And one may follow custom, etc. And where no clear custom — certainly forbid, for Beit Yosef wrote in name of most poskim to be stringent; and Maharshal ruled stringent in all cases.",
  "4#א": "They practice to forbid. Tosafot wrote in name of BeHag: since it stands at end eventually to split and puncture — good to be cautious, for their words are received tradition — end.",
  "4#ב": "And it must be flesh appearance surrounding; and if not, etc. Should read: through expertise they made flesh surround, etc.; meaning even though surround was not made until other examiners came and through great effort — nevertheless kosher as above; and Maharshal wrote: I saw in BeHag that flesh-thread lung appearance is not needed, only like small thread; and so appears to permit, for in many examinations I saw written even hair-thread; if so certainly no lung appearance; and further since many geonim permitted even without surrounding flesh — end; and according to first proof one could permit also in adjacent when flesh thread interrupts without lung appearance — except not to rely since adjacency treifot mentioned in Talmud, unlike slopes — as Maharshal in second proof.",
  "5#א": "Even though they do not pour, etc. Meaning we could have said it appears like two adjacent bubbles — he teaches it is not similar to adjacent; afterward Rama wrote from concern for bronchi it is worse when pouring.",
  "5#ב": "Meaning two fingerbreadths, etc. Meaning where lung is thick there are bronchi — until far from slopes two fingerbreadths in thin; and see what I write shortly in this seif on this law.",
  "5#ג": "And even clear water. His words are astonishing: in adjacent which is Talmudic law he wrote above one follows custom; and in slopes wrote law in clear water like adjacent; and here in across law which is only custom as poskim say — he decided to be stringent; and Maharshal wrote in name of Rosh of Vienna: since it is universal acceptance — do not be stringent in clear water; but water must be clear, not murky, sweet not putrid or salty, for murky, putrid, salty ruin bronchi and lung does not return; his words appear to permit even without bronchus examination, for clear water does not spoil; and further since extra stringency and most poskim did not mention, unlike slopes mentioned in Tosafot in name of BeHag — end; and so is primary; and Moharach z\"l also permitted in clear water; except in name of Maharshal he wrote to forbid even clear water — possibly he found thus in some manuscript there from him; but as I brought here in his name it is from his book Perek Aleph Tav siman 37.",
  "5#ד": "And there is bronchus, etc. I saw many examiners err in explaining this law — it was difficult: he wrote recognizable across — from whatever soul, if truly recognizable across what does he teach treifah; if not why truly treifah — I said to write explanation: the matter is bubble in slopes kosher if flesh thread surrounds — still treifah in that bubble from bubble recognizable across; rather necessarily to say there it does not disqualify from across since no bronchi as above seif 5 measure two fingers from thin place i.e. slopes; and on this he said here in varda it is not so, for even in thin place under varda there is bronchus at varda's groove; therefore if bubble found there — treifah if recognizable across even if flesh surrounds, since bronchi there — like its thick place; unlike other onot of lung which do not disqualify in their thin place since no bronchi; and if bubble in varda in thick place or its root — all the more treifah if recognizable across; but without recognizable across no treifah at all in varda like rest of lung. I saw Maharshal brought this law in name of Likutim and wrote it appears one should not be stringent in varda more than rest of lung, since many geonim permit even without varda at all — if so proven bronchi of lung are not primary for life to depend on them — end; his words very astonishing — he wanted varda bronchi stricter than other lung bronchi — we only came to say since there is bronchus even in thin place, law is to forbid when recognizable across; and so correct practically to be stringent as we wrote; and he said well here recognizable across to teach here forbidden from across like rest of lung; and we learn further: every bubble in slopes that was kosher if flesh surrounds — must see if it spreads down lung more than two fingers from slopes — then treifah from across; examiners must be warned — so simple and clear.",
  "5#ה": "Recognizable tinnir across, etc. Also here his words astonishing: why in adjacent and slopes whose treifot are clear to all — kosher in tinnir as above a fortiori across; and Maharshal also wrote he found written treifah but we do not heed, for reason I wrote; and so is primary practically; also in Machberet HaChayim testified they practice thus explicitly to permit.",
  "6#_": "Where slaughterer's hand did not feel. Implies but if he felt — rely to be lenient as siman 36 seif 5; and Darkei Moshe after this law: if he felt — kosher provided he examines ribs that no flaw in ribs — end; so found written in Beit Yosef siman 39 — brought responsum of R' Yosef son of Rosh: two years saw bubble in slopes, inflated, agreed no flesh surrounded; other examiners say they inflated and permitted, tore bubble, said latter had better inflation strength than first; he wrote he would not eat this meat; Beit Yosef wrote stringency he was stringent on him; by law animal kosher; and appears even Maharshal who ruled siman 1 seif 14 animal forbidden from witness contradiction — nevertheless admits here kosher, for we can answer no contradiction — certainly reasonable one knows to inflate better than fellow; even in capital cases we say reconcile witnesses all we can as mishnah beginning \"they would examine\"; therefore permitted even for us; and Rama brought here in Darkei Moshe; and Moharach wrote for us animal not examined lung lost — likewise forbidden here since contradiction; but as I wrote no contradiction; and explicitly siman 39 seif 5 if difference much inflation to little we go to permit; and so here; and siman 39 seif 17 I wrote even if contradiction — kosher — see there.",
};

export const baerHeitev = {
  "1#_": "Adjacent. And Shach wrote: even though above siman 36 regarding lung poured out the Rav wrote only in great loss permit murky and putrid — one must say there is also bronchus concern, unlike here (since bubble has pouch by itself and mugla did not touch bronchus. I found: old bubble — how treifah: when examiner puts hand to check and it dissolves in examiner's hand — moldy — treifah; and if type of lung bubbles they peel by hand and lung remains whole in bubble's place — treifah and inflation does not help, lest it was punctured in bubble place and healed and membrane from blow is not membrane. Kenesset HaGedolah daf 113).",
  "2#א": "Treifah. And so Taz and Shach: even bubble of clear water; and all the more complete adhesion adhered elsewhere emerging from bubble — pressing and feeling do not help; even from tinnir — it appears treifah; pressing and feeling do not help; even in onot we do not say lining protects.",
  "2#ב": "Treifah. And Taz wrote: from this examiners learned to declare treifah wherever two flaws; and not similar to hanging adhesion from tinnir kosher as below siman 39 seif 8 in hagahah; and must say because of tinnir no flaw there at all; and in hagahot R\"tz on examinations: hanging adhesion from bubble with clear water — kosher, for clear water not flaw; and it appears treifah. Taz wrote further: bubble emerging from adhesion between ona and ona below halfway — not called two flaws, for below halfway no adhesion; but if window there — though we permit as below siman 39 seif 4 — nevertheless poskim forbid even in window; and here further bubble flaw — at least two flaws treifah; and bubble from adhesion between ona and ama below halfway even without window — some hold that adhesion treifah — nevertheless here two flaws. Incident: lung adhered to pouch, adhesion full blood until around adhesion to pouch all blood appearance — I declared treifah, worse than two flaws — pressing does not help (large bubble like nut on middle ona of right on ribs, protruding outward, no lung adhesion except root that was adhered — rest outside; Shach siman 25 declared treifah and Pri Chadash agreed, but not for my reason). And Shach wrote: if bubble skin changes to lung appearance even on protrusion or other flaw — kosher, for lung appearance — only internal deficiency.",
  "3#א": "Forbidden. And the reason: they are adjacent only from puncture in lung.",
  "3#ב": "And kosher. Taz in name of Maharshal: still requires examination whether each has pouch by itself — treifah even if pouring (and this is what they ask: how find lung-appearance break between bubble and bubble yet treifah though pouring: if punctured and did not pour and afterward inflated this one and fellow rose in inflation, or put water in one and fellow filled — kosher like two marot siman 43 — Kenesset HaGedolah daf 114).",
  "3#ג": "Tzemachim. Meaning hard tzemachim is tinnir and no moisture at all (and same full of air kosher in adjacent — Shach and Bach).",
  "3#ד": "Lung. Taz wrote this hagahah belongs elsewhere even adjacent kosher; Maharshal's reason: morsa kosher — not called bubble but outward protrusion; implies mugla in morsa — nevertheless does not forbid adjacent. Shach wrote: some explain morsa is called in Italian moisture inside like turquoise appearance, grow between skin and flesh — membrane has no lung appearance only morsa — kosher; not clear — if no lung membrane covering — adjacent treifah? And wrote: specifically when lung membrane covers and not higher than lung; but if high — forbids in adjacency even without tarfa de-asa or ona form.",
  "3#ה": "Lung appearance. Taz explained: but if mugla appearance — like adjacent treifah; and found written: if upper bubble skin peeled — lung skin — treifah, for lower is bubble skin from blow — even single bubble, even clear water.",
  "3#ו": "And sweet. Shach explained: exclude bitter or salty like murky; sign what is clear water: pouch by itself, peels from lung, no wind when puncturing, white skin inside (Pri Chadash: when examining bubbles poke with thorn not knife — iron spoils water; receive only in vessel not hand — see Api Ravrevi). Shach wrote this sign helps even for us; nevertheless requires study; Semachot strained.",
  "3#ז": "Distance. Shach wrote Maharshal disagrees with custom — view one may not permit even in great loss; Bach likewise; therefore appears what Rav wrote \"or according to loss and pressure\" — specifically where both; not as Pri Megadim \"or time of pressure.\"",
  "3#ח": "In adjacent. Meaning where prohibit clear water in adjacent — same in slopes; where permit — permit; but surrounding thread — not similar, for all agree in slopes one hair suffices.",
  "3#ט": "Treifah. Meaning bubble on upper right ona in groove place.",
  "3#י": "Adjacent. Shach wrote: accordingly in clear water lenient where lenient; however another reason — concern friction on small ribs and gargeret — good to be stringent (and if membrane covers bubble even on groove — no grain-friction concern, for meat covers bubble and covering meat must have lung appearance. Rama's distinction between two bubbles and bubble with tinnir: tinnir punctures bubble even without pressing; unlike two bubbles that do not puncture each other except through pressing; therefore kosher between onot with gap. Rama bubble and tinnir adjacent kosher — Pri Chadash unclear: since adjacent bubbles treifah from pressing, all the more bubble and tinnir — tinnir hard and punctures; Shach forbids; Kenesset HaGedolah brings in name of several poskim to permit — and so practice in examinations).",
  "4#א": "To forbid. Reason in Shach: appears like two adjacent bubbles, marit ayin concern; Taz wrote reason: stands at end to split and puncture; Pri Chadash wrote all lung ends even from sides called slopes, for lung in animal hung not lay — so on all sides hung and stands, end to split and puncture.",
  "4#ב": "Lung. Maharshal permits even without lung appearance (since only measure one thread — certainly no lung appearance; and since many geonim lenient in slope bubble — lenient; if lost before checking surrounding flesh — permit — Likutim 29 and Kenesset HaGedolah daf 118). Taz wrote: accordingly could permit also in adjacent with flesh interrupting without lung appearance — except not to rely since adjacency treifot in Talmud, unlike slopes lenient — end.",
  "4#ג": "Well. Meaning even through great effort (and if membrane tears from this inflation — treifah).",
  "5#א": "To change. Shach wrote: specifically in general animals these measures; but if see bronchi outside measures — treifah; Lev Chaim wrote implies we do not care for bronchi at edge outside measures.",
  "5#ב": "In bubble. Maharshal and Taz disagree with Rama and permit clear water; Shach (and so Noda Biyehudah) disagrees — primary like Rama to forbid (examination does not help).",
  "5#ג": "And putrid. Reason in Shach: then not like poured like pitcher — no bronchus concern.",
  "5#ד": "Across. Taz wrote: even if flesh surrounds — teaches here: in ona flesh if bubble in slopes with flesh between — all the more kosher; reason: no bronchi there, unlike varda where bronchus (at varda groove); all the more in thick place or root — treifah (if recognizable across; without across no treifah in varda like rest of lung). Unlike Maharshal who disagrees with Rama and permits varda; and wrote warn examiners: every slope bubble kosher with surround — see if spreads down more than two fingers from slopes — then treifah from across — end.",
  "5#ה": "Like bubbles. Taz wrote they practice permission in this law (and so primary Shach, Pri Chadash).",
  "6#_": "Treifah (we do not surround bubbles — bubbles change — Shach; see Api Ravrevi). Taz wrote: but if he felt — rely lenient as siman 36 seif 5; must examine ribs; also incident Beit Yosef siman 39 — two saw slope bubble, inflated, agreed no surround; others inflated, permitted, tore, said better strength — Bach wrote for us unexamined animal forbidden; Taz: we can answer no contradiction, one inflates better — permitted; Moharach wrote unexamined forbidden — contradiction; but as I wrote no contradiction; siman 39 seif 5, 17 — even contradiction kosher (Beit Yosef, Darkei Moshe).",
  "7#_": "Kosher. Pri Chadash proved: if adhered in all limbs to place puncture disqualifies — every treifah; nevertheless if heart or spleen adhered to support elsewhere — do not declare treifah, for who says puncture reaches disqualifying place — only external flaw, not inside.",
};

export const kafHachayim = {
  "1#_": "A) Seif 1: lung with blisters, etc.; putrid moisture — treifah. Hagahah: many permit murky and putrid — meaning very large bubbles, not concerned for bronchus examination — Taz s.k. 1. And even though above siman 36 seif 7 lung poured — Rav in hagahah only great loss permits murky and putrid — one may say there bronchus concern if not melted, unlike here lung not so impaired — Shach s.k. 1; Pri Chadash ot 1; Likutim 29 ot 2; Lev Chaim ot 2; Shulchan Gavoah ot 1; Beit Yisrael ot 2; see below ot 12.",
  "2#_": "B) There hagahah: many permit, etc.; custom permit bubbles in every case if not adjacent, even without great loss — Kenesset HaGedolah in Hagahot Beit Yosef ot 9; Pri Chadash ot 2; Pri Torah ot 1; wrote all acharonim raised, unlike Maran in Shulchan Aruch — Likutim there; Shulchan Gavoah ot 3; wrote so practiced in kingdom of Hungary and everywhere we heard — never heard anywhere they checked bubble water for murky or putrid, only kidney; except Jerusalem where they check lung bubbles like kidney bubbles — because they accepted Maran's ruling — see there; and so Semachot ot 1: custom in these lands (Ashkenaz) permit even murky, putrid, salty water or putrid moisture — do not deviate; but where no custom — forbid. And so Pri Tevuah ot 3; Beit Yisrael ot 1; Yad Yitzchak part 1 ot 1; MeZah siman 31 ot 1; Eitz Yosef siman 16 ot 1; Kometz HaMinchah general rule 21 ot 1; Zivchei Tzedek siman 10 ot 1; Minchat Yitzchak branch 1 ot 1; and Zivchei Tzedek ot 1: in their place (Yemen) practiced leniently as hagahah; and Turei Zahav siman 10 ot 2; Zivchei Tzvi ot 1 — wrote custom in Baghdad — see there.",
  "3#_": "C) What he wrote: in Jerusalem they check, etc. — Sephardic custom; but Ashkenazim in Jerusalem practice as our teacher z\"l — no issue of lo titgodedu — see our words Orach Chaim siman 468 — see there.",
  "4#_": "D) In places that declare treifah — open every bubble in lung and check for disqualifiers; if clear water — taste if sweet; bitter or salty — law like murky and putrid. Even not protruding bubble, only morsa level with rest of lung — stringent without great loss. If lost before knowing clear or murky — permit in great loss or pressure; if saw clear and did not taste before lost — lenient. If many bubbles — open all, do not rely on majority tested clear; if opened all clear and tasted majority sweet — enough, need not taste more; if opened majority clear, did not finish all before lost — lenient — Pri Tevuah ot 3, 4; Beit Yisrael in Levushei Serad there; Minchat Yitzchak there ot 2; see below end ot 6.",
  "5#_": "E) Measure when called putrid, bitter, or full — not explained in poskim; appears must be unfit for human drinking except under pressure — Pri Tevuah siman 36 ot 83; Beit Yisrael in Levushei Serad there; see below ot 99.",
  "6#_": "F) Do not puncture with knife but thorn — knife makes water salty and wrong treifah; do not dip finger in bubbles and touch finger — finger flesh embitters; lick tongue from water to test taste — Kenesset HaGedolah in Hagahot Tur ot 28. What Kenesset HaGedolah wrote there: if many bubbles from clear water, test one — known all clear — Beit David Rafa\"f there ot 4 wrote acharonim disagree; therefore Pri Tevuah ruled as above ot 4 — see there; see below ot 100.",
  "7#_": "G) There hagahah: many permit murky, etc. In non-Jew's animal — proper to be stringent like Rif and Rambam, forbid murky and putrid; in Jew's animal rely on Rashba and Rosh and permit; because of butcher's embarrassment or slaughterer's wage or share from kosher not treifah, or giving gentile owner 3-4 lungs called Israel's property — Kenesset HaGedolah Hagahot Beit Yosef ot 8; Shulchan Gavoah Machazik ot 1; wrote on this Aloniki practiced permit bubbles even murky putrid water in gentile's animal because embarrassment or wage called their property; so custom in Adrian — Mahari\"t — end; and Turei Zahav siman 10 ot 2; Zivchei Tzvi ot 2 — wrote custom Baghdad permit even gentile's animal because community tax from kosher — see below siman 9 ot 200.",
};

export const pitcheiTeshuva = {
  "1#_": "Treifah. Avodat HaTaharah; and what he wrote in name of Taz and Shach — even bubble of clear water. Examiner in Shach s.k. 3 will see he did not write thus except explaining Mechaber's words, but for law he inclines lenient; and so his words taught in Noda Biyehudah. [See responsum Mishkenot Yaakov siman 17: from Mahariu's examinations clear like Shach — hanging from within bubble not stricter than two adjacent; explicit in responsum Mahar\"an part 3 siman 105 and Penei Yehoshua siman 12; and Beit Ephraim ruled at start of his pamphlet: two flaws — where custom lenient adjacent in clear water, same for hanging — unlike Taz. And see there incident in community: middle right ona larger than lower, bubble on it clear water, custom permit two adjacent in clear water, exchanges of Rama (siman 35 seif 1) plainly permit — posek ruled permit and done on his word; one rav appealed permit because two flaws and declared vessels treifah too; he expanded posek ruled well because exchange-flaw for permitters is lighter than hanging adhesion flaw; since many permit hanging adhesion from bubble in clear water — all the more exchange; unless murky or hanging adhesion found on exchanges — clear there forbid. And wrote on punctures found in this lung — not needed to answer since examiner elsewhere than ona, not adjacent — certainly no two flaws; but per that rav examiner was on exchange ona — discuss; nevertheless can incline permit — see there.] And see in Dagul MeRevavah: nevertheless it appears two adjacent in clear water and hanging adhesion from one — certainly treifah from two flaws even where custom permits adjacent alone in clear water. Further wrote there: appears from R\"tz's precision clear water not flaw, also not for hanging adhesion emerging not adhered elsewhere — implies if adhered elsewhere — considered flaw even with clear water, pressing and feeling do not help — see there. [See Torat Chesed siman 36: Semachot siman 39 seif 47 — hanging adhesion from bubble covered by lung flesh kosher even higher than lung; adhered elsewhere treifah if high — not better than adhesion on protrusion adhered elsewhere — obvious two flaws like bubble on protrusion — end; he wrote Gaon's comparison unclear — what connection high bubble to protrusion; protrusion is slight flesh flaw, if adhesion joins elsewhere treifah; unlike bubble covered by lung flesh — only internal deficiency, height from mugla inside will exit through slope — no flaw; my view to permit in all cases — see there.] See Givat Shaul siman 41: asked lung with adhesion passing through pressing and feeling, adhesion where upper skin slightly peeled — answered forbid two flaws like adhesion from bubble — see at length. See responsum Har HaCarmel part 10 siman 2, end siman 3; Pri Tevuah siman 38, 39 [and responsum Torat Chesed siman 36 at length] what they wrote on two flaws — see there.",
  "2#_": "Treifah. Avodat HaTaharah; see responsum Beit Ephraim part 10 siman 11: adhesion adhered emerging from red appearance, appearance returns to lung by inflation — is it two flaws — see there. What Avodat HaTaharah wrote in name of Taz — incident lung adhered to pouch, etc. — see responsum Beit Ephraim siman 19: simple same law for hanging adhesion full of blood — treifah even if after removing hanging adhesion underneath whole and fine, examine, does not bubble — still treifah even in great loss and pressure, for certainly puncture here — see at length.",
  "3#_": "[Lung appearance. Avodat HaTaharah; see Beit Ephraim s.k. 11: even if gap between them, if no lung appearance on it — law of adjacency on bubbles — see there; brought also Me'irat Einayim and Etz Levonah — see there.]",
  "4#_": "And they feel. See responsum Maharit part 2 siman 11: asked slope bubble they did not manage to press and inflate to see flesh surround until torn — what law? Answered: his view — entire law that if through feeling flesh surrounds — kosher only where without inflation it appeared as flesh surrounds, and when inflated bubble revealed and flesh slipped — then they said feel; but if without inflation no surround — do not feel at all; language proves Beit Yosef: if inflated and no surround, etc.; therefore this one they did not feel and inflate — if before inflation appears no surround — obviously treifah even if not examined; but if initially appears surround yet needs inflation whether holds afterward — restore presumption of permission. See responsum Maggid MeReishit part 2 siman 2: animal with bubble in slope of ona, did not see if surround, inflated, no surround; expert came, through feeling made surround — what law? Brought Maharit's words — imply in our case forbid since unknown before inflation was surround; raised: since primary slope bubble law not in Gemara — interpret all his words leniently — Rav only spoke his case where slope examiners forbid without surround; but slope of ona examiners permit; and Rav z\"l only spoke where they saw before inflation no surround; but if before inflation not seen and after feeling raised surround — restore presumption of permission; three rabbis agreed permit that animal; they inclined permit even if certainly no surround before inflation, since Beit Yosef and Rama unlike Maharit — listen to be lenient in this law — see there.",
  "5#_": "The slopes in thin. See Turei Zahav: all agree here slopes means bottom; but in other sharp points and ends bronchi begin immediately; see responsum Har HaCarmel part 10 siman 4 disagrees and raised: in entire law measure distance of bronchi from sharp point like at bottom — see there.",
};

export const yadEphraim = {
  "1#_": "If they are not adjacent. Avodat HaTaharah; see responsum Beit Yosef in Sluchovitz full 47 standing on lung protruding outward.",
  "2#_": "Emerging from bubble — treifah. Avodat HaTaharah; responsum Penei Yehoshua siman 13: lung with drippings and strands hanging, Sluchovitz hanging on drippings — do not judge as slope bubble, for its place is drippings; remove drippings with Sluchovitz — lung whole; slope bubble itself extra stringency. Also not hanging from bubble unless bubble itself lung as imagined from \"raised tzemachim\"; but bubble hanging from adhesion — we did not hear. Further: since we hold adjacent in clear water kosher — same here; clear water not called bubble but Sluchovitz; even partly mugla like needle-head follow majority — not called bubble except majority mugla. Reason also supports: since so moist, if from puncture would adhere elsewhere as Beit Yosef — therefore permit — see there; see Beit Ephraim siman 39 s.k. 10, 115; Beur Zahav Gold end siman 39 explains there too: such case only strands and strands, bubble of clear water kosher; specifically thick adhesion or large button full mugla — see there.",
  "3#_": "Sound discipline treifah. Avodat HaTaharah; from Taz's words all around filled blood appearance (I wrote scribal error — should be all around it blood appearance, etc.); in my responsum Beit Ephraim part 2 manuscript I wrote: adhesion inside protruding bubble below halfway between ona and ama with window, bubble not covered, salty water inside, adhesion passed through proper pressing, checked in lukewarm, did not bubble — see my laws of two flaws seif 6; from there see leniency in such case in great loss — requires study, specifically bubble not of clear water; even of clear water where custom stringent on hanging even from clear water; but where custom lenient on hanging from clear water — lenient here in slight loss. What I wrote there seif 5 in murky water — stringent — refers to ona passed through pressing; also as I think missing in print and omission — should be: if bubble of murky water where custom stringent on bubble i.e. murky water — stringent and forbid. See my books: pillars of world Beit Ephraim and Magen Shmuel permit below halfway even without pressing, all the more with pressing; though my books' implication I did not rely to lenient on adhesion ona to ama with window — nevertheless per reason I wrote there flaws do not oppose and pressing applies — I permitted in great loss and Shabbat honor; but per one who asked question — no pressing, only detachment from one side — since Shach's father and Shach stringent — who will dare be lenient — see there. See my responsum Beit Ephraim siman 19: thin hanging adhesion on upper ona, they pressed adhesion off lung, wiped blood after pressing, blood exited afterward, still did not bubble in test, great loss, many animals declared treifah — simple complete treifah, permitter liable karet, vessels forbidden; even if blood did not return after wiping; to eye whole and fine after removing adhesion, test does not bubble — treifah: if no puncture — whence blood? Even without adhesion, drops of blood on lung — wipe, four drops return — certainly treifah though test there does not bubble; even make doubt red sweat — do not make; vanity of vanities, especially after slaughter obvious no drops if membranes whole — simple throughout Israel to forbid when lung exudes blood; a fortiori with adhesion as question; test not bubbling does not permit — see there; but if did not watch lung immediately and blood found — can attribute to hand feeling — room to permit as I wrote Beit Ephraim siman 1 and Kaf HaChaim there — see there. Once I happened in that place; slaughterers told great distress: common on upper ona thin red hanging adhesion; when pressed off lung blood on lung — great loss. They said certainly adhesion adheres inside only because place narrow and adhesion very thin detaches from connection, remains adhered to lung — I ordered if occurs bring before pressing; they did — I saw adhesion on place where bronchus near membrane, membrane very thin no hold in flesh; slaughterers quickly press by hand — even walking lightly, membrane weakness makes fine puncture from snatching thin adhesion — blood exits; I ordered cut entire upper ona, placed in lukewarm water bowl, pressed and felt gently quarter hour to soften adhesion, removed, ordered expert press adhesion not quick customary way but much patience — through softening came off easily, no mark, no blood; inflated upper ona through bronchus, lukewarm test, no bubble — I permitted. I said how great sages' words — lukewarm softens adhesion; as Azrieli responsum siman 39 s.k. 15 — test: leave in lukewarm to soften; Ran's reason for lukewarm on lung adjacent to lining — if you ask all explanations — through soaking in lukewarm it tears and puncture revealed; Taz thought must leave lung in lukewarm and soak. Though in my work I wondered on Taz and Azrieli and poskim — Ran's primary intent not remove adhesion with weak-mouthed knife lest spoil and wrongly treifah — leave in lukewarm to soften and detach itself, then know if puncture — siman 39. Nevertheless Ran teaches soaking in lukewarm adhesion detaches easier from lung; I wrote so expert slaughterers hear — if occurs do not hurry feeling; though saliva on adhesion at pressing time — still wait for softening action; saliva spreads sideways — better do as I wrote. If no expert to inflate upper ona alone — do not cut, place whole lung in large vessel water floating on adhesion, feel gently long as estimated softened; good not remove by pressing until lift from water — lest blood drop unnoticed; if adhesion fully removes no blood, test inflate lukewarm no bubble — permit as I wrote; do only expert God-fearing slaughterer gathering all experts — must be careful on lukewarm and heat not contract, and inflation proper; since incident came — good inform public gate, for Torah spares Israel's money.",
  "4#_": "They practice to forbid. Avodat HaTaharah; see responsum Ohel Yaakov siman 12: bubble between Sephardic cuts — custom cuts not called slopes; in Fez more lenient — say only slopes of ama; cannot decide — all depends prior custom to permit — do not declare treifah — see there; see my books all explained well.",
  "5#_": "Recognizable tinnir across. Avodat HaTaharah; see responsum Chavot Binyamin siman 44: goose lung bubble across; brought Beit Ephraim siman 37 — see there.",
  "6#_": "Except lung kosher. Avodat HaTaharah; see Chavat Yair siman 76: thin adhered to one another — permit, for adhesion only in lung; all the more here though Taz forbade only adhesion to lining or elsewhere; likewise mara and similar irregular adhesion — unlike thin adhered to one another in order — see Beit Ephraim siman 39 from s.k. 196 onward.",
};
